{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778781027,"nonce":"xhRULHo+IMocUSEmZJYcw9EzA04=","title":"Lazy-import ipywidgets inside PlotlyFigureWidget so web backend does not require the notebook extra","message":"The web backend boot path imports `feedbax.database` -\u003e `feedbax.web.api.figures` -\u003e `feedbax.plot_utils`, which currently does an unconditional top-level `import ipywidgets as widgets` (plot_utils.py:9).\n\n`ipywidgets` is declared under the optional `notebook` extra in pyproject.toml (line 70), so `uv sync` (without extras) does not install it. The result: any attempt to run `uvicorn feedbax.web.app:app` fails with `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named ipywidgets`.\n\nAudit of usage:\n- `ipywidgets as widgets` is referenced ONLY inside `class PlotlyFigureWidget` (plot_utils.py:226) - a Jupyter notebook display helper with Copy-PNG / Copy-JSON buttons.\n- `PlotlyFigureWidget` is NEVER imported or instantiated anywhere in the codebase (verified via repo-wide grep). It is dead weight for the web app and for headless runs.\n- The web backend only consumes `savefig` from `plot_utils`.\n\nFix:\n1. Remove the top-level `import ipywidgets as widgets` from `feedbax/plot_utils.py`.\n2. Move the import inside `PlotlyFigureWidget.__init__` (or `create_widgets`), so it is only required when the notebook helper is actually used.\n3. After the fix, `uv run uvicorn feedbax.web.app:app --port 8000` should start cleanly without the `notebook` extra installed.\n\nTest: importing `feedbax.web.app` in a Python REPL with the current (notebook-extra-free) venv must succeed.","files":null}]}